# One datagram per line, in the shapes UniFi's remote syslog sends them; the
# \n that ends a line is the line feed that ends the datagram. Every name and
# address is a placeholder: hosts, clients and policies are invented, IP
# addresses are from the documentation ranges (192.0.2.0/24, 198.51.100.0/24,
# 203.0.113.0/24), MAC addresses from 00:00:5e:00:53:00/24.

# An access point, a daemon's line: the tag is "<mac>,<model>-<firmware>", and
# the program is named twice.
<30>Nov 15 15:54:46 Attic 00005e005301,UAP-nanoHD-6.7.57+15670: mcad: mcad[15140]: wireless_agg_stats.log_sta_anomalies(): bssid=00:00:5e:00:53:02 radio=ra0 vap=ra3 sta=00:00:5e:00:53:10 satisfaction_now=79 anomalies=tcp_latency\n

# An access point, a kernel line: no pid.
<4>Nov 15 15:54:49 Attic 00005e005301,UAP-nanoHD-6.7.57+15670: kernel: [583602.192961] ra3: Send NULL to STA-00:00:5e:00:53:11 idle(60) timeout(180)\n

# An access point, the first of the two program names left empty.
<14>Nov 15 16:05:20 Attic 00005e005301,UAP-nanoHD-6.7.57+15670: : wevent[11718]: wevent.ubnt_custom_event(): EVENT_STA_JOIN ra3: 00:00:5e:00:53:31 / 14\n

# The gateway: its own name where the program's belongs, then "<program>[pid]:".
<14>Nov 15 15:54:49 Gateway Gateway mcad[4588]: udapi-cfg._udapi_lu_set_inform_interval(): Changing LU inform interval 1 -> 20 (cur-state=ON)\n

# The gateway, a message that starts with spaces and holds runs of them.
<30>Nov 15 15:55:15 Gateway Gateway earlyoom[1838]:   psi cpu  some avg10= 4.59% avg60= 7.33%\n

# The gateway's firewall log: a policy's block between two networks, UDP. The
# line ends with a space.
<13>Nov 15 16:08:42 Gateway Gateway [LAN_LAN-D-10004] DESCR="Block Visitors to Family" IN=br4 OUT=br2 MAC=00:00:5e:00:53:01:00:00:5e:00:53:20:08:00 SRC=192.0.2.16 DST=198.51.100.170 LEN=32 TOS=00 PREC=0x00 TTL=63 ID=30555 PROTO=UDP SPT=3722 DPT=3722 LEN=12 MARK=0x21940000 \n

# The gateway's firewall log: a port forward, TCP, no outbound interface yet,
# a bracket inside the policy's name, flags among the fields.
<13>Nov 15 16:05:23 Gateway Gateway [PREROUTING-DNAT-2] DESCR="PortForward DNAT [Web]" IN=br2 OUT= MAC=00:00:5e:00:53:01:00:00:5e:00:53:21:08:00 SRC=192.0.2.150 DST=203.0.113.244 LEN=64 TOS=18 PREC=0xA0 TTL=64 ID=0 PROTO=TCP SPT=59910 DPT=8443 SEQ=880678430 ACK=0 WINDOW=65535 SYN URGP=0 MARK=0x21940000 \n

# The console's events are CEF, with no <priority> at their head. A firewall
# block, ICMP, so no ports; values hold spaces and parentheses.
Nov 15 16:04:29 Gateway CEF:0|Ubiquiti|UniFi Network|10.6.109|203|Blocked by Firewall|4|UNIFIcategory=Security UNIFIhost=Gateway proto=ICMP act=blocked UNIFIrisk=low UNIFIpolicyName=Block Plugs to External UNIFIpolicyType=Firewall UNIFIdirection=outgoing deviceInboundInterface=Devices deviceOutboundInterface=Uplink (WAN1) dst=203.0.113.100 UNIFIsrcClientAlias=Porch Plug UNIFIsrcClientHostname=plug UNIFIsrcClientIp=192.0.2.168 UNIFIsrcClientMac=00:00:5e:00:53:30 UNIFIsrcClientModel=Smart Plug Mini UNIFIsrcZone=Internal UNIFIdstRegion=US UNIFIdstZone=External UNIFIfirewallPolicy=Block Plugs to External UNIFItotalBytes=84 UNIFItotalPackets=1 UNIFIflowCount=1 UNIFIflowId=null UNIFIutcTime=2026-11-16T00:04:29.427Z msg=Porch Plug was blocked from accessing 203.0.113.100 by the Block Plugs to External Firewall Policy.\n

